      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since `CBUILD` is not set when you run `make` locally, we would still need to account for the `-` or `BUILD_CC` would expand to `-gcc`. Something like:\n\n```\nifeq ($(CBUILD),)\nCBUILD\u003dx86_64-pc-linux-gnu-\nelse\nCBUILD\u003d$(CBUILD)-\nendif\n```\n\nThe main reason that I used `BUILDCC_PREFIX` was to try to keep the naming consistent with other variables that you can override when building (`HOST_CROSS_COMPILE`, `CROSS_COMPILE`). Those variables are distinct from the equivalent portage variables (`CHOST`, `CTARGET`).\n\nI don\u0027t have strong feelings though, so I can change it if you think it\u0027s clearer.",
